Explanation of the change:

- Previously the canvas was always sized at `devicePixelRatio × viewportSize`.  
- Since we request the image itself at `devicePixelRatio` (and thus its own `imagePixelRatio` reflects that), we only need `(devicePixelRatio / imagePixelRatio)` to map view pixels to canvas pixels.  
- This reduces the memory footprint by the square of that ratio on HiDPI.
